      "writtenOn": "2026-09-09T13:28:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No — the K6 tests would not catch broken logging. They drive the CPS HTTP\n  API and assert on status codes and latency; they only archive pod logs for\n  post-mortem inspection, never asserting on log content or that appenders are\n  attached. A pod with completely broken logging would still pass every K6\n  scenario. This is precisely the gap this test closes: it loads the real\n  logback-spring.xml and asserts the root logger has an appender attached, for\n  both console and json formats.",
      "parentUuid": "440aa5ca_08322009",
      "revId": "53d438526dc3aa80782c594098ae016ecdbdc3a8",
      "serverId": "14b4e41f-c4e3-4fb9-9955-6a9b5656895a"
